@bio:

	Ewa Dahlig-Turek is an ethnomusicologist and professor at
	the Institute of Art of the Polish Academy of Sciences. Her
	research focuses on traditional musical culture in Poland,
	especially bowed chordophones and the morphology of “Polish
	rhythms” in Polish and Scandinavian traditional music.
	Since her research stay at the Universität-Hochschule Essen
	in 1992/1993, she has developed Music Information Retrieval
	methods. Since 1994, she has led the EsAC project, creating
	databases used internationally. In 2023, with
	collaborators, she completed an electronic edition of
	around 20,000 musical notations from Oskar Kolberg’s
	<i>Complete Works</i> and co-created webEsAC.

@@END: BIO